# Dragon Quest VII Reimagined (PPSA17942) — title -> new adventure log -> name entry ->
# first-run System Settings -> opening chapter -> FREE FIELD CONTROL in Pilchard Bay.
#
# The difference from reach-gameplay.pad is one thing only, and it is not a new control:
# HOW MANY confirms the opening chapter is given. That route advances dialogue every 15 s
# and never leaves the script; this one presses every 2 s and reaches free field control at
# t~600 s. Measured over three runs on the same binary, quiet box, world phase only:
#
#     confirms delivered   frames with the field HUD
#     41                   1
#     37                   1
#     447                  145        (t=600..1236 s)
#
# So the chapter script was never a wall — it is long, and the earlier routes ran out of
# patience rather than out of road. Nothing here depends on a lucky press landing on a
# particular screen: every screen in the chapter waits indefinitely for confirm, so a press
# that arrives early is simply absorbed.
#
# Read scripts/dragon-quest-vii/README.md for the control model before editing the part
# above 320 s — OPTIONS is the jump-to-OK shortcut on the name keyboard, and the two System
# Settings menus have DIFFERENT row counts.

# first-run System Settings -> opening chapter in Estard (T001).
#
# The first seven pulses are reach-title-screen.pad unchanged; everything after 35 s was
# derived by watching a live-reloaded route (PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_RELOAD=1) frame by frame.
# Read scripts/dragon-quest-vii/README.md for the control model before editing this:
# in particular OPTIONS is the jump-to-OK shortcut on the name keyboard, and the two
# System Settings menus have DIFFERENT row counts, so the down-counts are not the same.
3:cross
6:cross
9:cross
12:cross
15:cross
18:cross
30:cross
# title is up by ~34 s
35:cross
# "Create a new adventure log" -> the slot list, with "1: Unused" highlighted
55:cross
# confirm the slot -> the player-name keyboard, cursor on 'A'
75:cross
# enter one character
100:cross
# OPTIONS jumps the cursor to the on-screen OK cell (cross alone never leaves the grid)
120:options
# OK -> "Are you happy to proceed with the name 'A'?", Yes preselected
140:cross
# Yes
160:cross
# System Settings 1/4: intro message
180:cross
# 1/4: character voice language, English preselected
195:cross
# 2/4: play style, Happy Medium preselected
210:cross
# 3/4: camera menu — FOUR rows (vertical axis / horizontal axis / revert / confirm).
# Cross on a row only toggles that row's value, so walk down to Confirm first.
230:down
238:down
246:down
254:cross
# 4/4: brightness menu — THREE rows (bar / revert / confirm). One fewer down than 3/4;
# a third down wraps back to the bar.
270:down
278:down
286:cross
# "Adventure log successfully created." -> the save is written and the level load starts
305:cross
320:cross
# opening chapter CS_CP1_001_010 and the walk into Estard; keep advancing dialogue

# ---- mash confirm through the opening chapter ----------------------------------
# 2 s spacing, not 15. This is the whole difference.
